## What you can do instead  

You can stay at a beachfront hotel (so you have the sea right at your door) and still reach the Picasso Museum with a short walk or a quick ride on public transport. Below are the best‑rated beachfront options that are the **closest** to the museum, together with the approximate walking distance and the easiest way to get there.

| Hotel (Beachfront) | Address | Approx. distance to Picasso Museum* | Typical travel time to museum |
|--------------------|---------|--------------------------------------|--------------------------------|
| **Hotel Arts Barcelona** | Marina, 19‑21 Boulevard de la Marina, 08005 Barcelona | ~1.9 km | 10‑minute walk along the waterfront **or** 5‑minute Metro (L4 → Barceloneta → Jaume I) |
| **W Barcelona** | Plaça de la Rosa dels Vents, 1, 08039 Barcelona | ~2.0 km | 12‑minute walk along the beach **or** Metro L4 to Barceloneta → Jaume I (≈5 min) |
| **Hotel 54 Barceloneta** | Carrer de la Marina, 54, 08003 Barcelona | ~1.6 km | 8‑minute walk along the promenade **or** V15 bus (≈5 min) |
| **Hotel Barcelona Princess** | Avinguda del Litoral, 62, 08005 Barcelona | ~1.8 km | 10‑minute walk **or** Metro L4 to Barceloneta → Jaume I (≈5 min) |

\*Distances are measured “as‑the‑crow‑flies” from the hotel’s main entrance to the museum (Carrer Montcada 15). All of these hotels let you step out onto the beach in seconds and still reach the museum in **under 15 minutes** by foot or a single public‑transport hop.

### Why these hotels?

* **Beachfront location** – direct sea view, private beach access or a terrace that looks out over the Mediterranean.  
* **Proximity to the city centre** – they sit just a few blocks north of the historic Gothic Quarter, so you can explore Barcelona’s main sights (La Rambla, Barri Gòtic, El Born) on foot.  
* **Good transport links** – all are on or next to Metro line 4 (the “yellow” line), which stops at **Jaume I** (the closest station to the Picasso Museum).  

If you prefer a hotel that is **right in the El Born district** (the museum’s neighbourhood) you’ll have to give up the beachfront. In that case, consider boutique options such as **Hotel Banys Orientals**, **Hotel Brummell**, or **Hotel Rec Barcelona**, which are within a 5‑minute walk of the museum but a few blocks inland from the sea.

---

## Nearby coastal towns you can visit after Barcelona  

Once you’ve enjoyed the museum and the beach, the Catalan coastline offers several charming towns that are perfect for day‑trips or an extra night‑stay. All are reachable by **Rodalies (regional) train** or **commuter bus** from Barcelona’s Sants, Passeig de Gràcia, or Estació de França stations.

| Town (≈ distance from Barcelona) | Typical travel time (train/bus) | What to see / do |
|----------------------------------|--------------------------------|-------------------|
| **Sitges** – 35 km SW | 30 min (R2 Sud) or 30 min by bus (V13) | Vibrant promenade, art galleries, nightlife, Sitges Film Festival (late June) |
| **Badalona** – 10 km NE | 12 min (R1) or 15 min by bus (V13) | Long sandy beach, historic old town, Torre del Rellotge |
| **Castelldefels** – 22 km SW | 25 min (R2 Sud) or 30 min by bus (V15) | Wide beach, water‑sports centre, Castelldefels Castle |
| **Mataró** – 30 km NE | 30 min (R1) | Roman ruins (Mataró Roman Villa), modernist architecture, long beach |
| **Vilanova i la Geltrú** – 45 km SW | 40 min (R2 Sud) | Seaside promenade, historic quarter, maritime museum |
| **Gavà** – 20 km SW | 20 min (R2 Sud) | Quiet coves, Parc Natural del Garraf, historic castle |
| **Sant Pol de Mar** – 45 km NE | 45 min (R1) | Small fishing village, beautiful bay, relaxed vibe |

### How to get there

| Transport | Ticket type | Approx. cost (single) |
|-----------|-------------|-----------------------|
| **Rodalies (Cercanías) train** | “T‑10” (10‑trip) or “Hola Barcelona” travel card (2‑day, 3‑day, 5‑day) | €2.40‑€4.80 per trip (depends on zones) |
| **Commuter bus (e.g., V13, V15)** | Same travel cards as above | €2.40‑€4.80 per trip |

All of the towns listed have **beachfront promenades** and a relaxed atmosphere that contrasts nicely with Barcelona’s bustling city centre.

